#git commands

# git flow
Working Directory → Staging Area → Local Repository → Remote Repository
      (edit)          (git add)       (git commit)      (git push)

Working directory - where i am currently modifying the files
staging area - the area between working directory and local repo whcih contains exact set of changes to include in the next commit. 
local repo - local repo is .git directory. it is like a database inside the project.


git clone
git pull - pulls the changes from remote repo to working directory (use git pull when you are ready to integrate changes immediately)
git fetch - fetches the changes from remote repo to local repo.( To review changes firt use git fetch) 
git add . (stages the changes from working directory to staging area)
git status
git commit -m "message" (commits the changes from staging to local repo)
git push (push the changes from local repo to remote repo)

git branch (lists all branches)
git branch branchname(creates a new branch)
git checkout branchname(checkout to that specific branch)
git branch -d branchname (deletes the mentioned branch)

# use merge for main, release, production.
# use git rebase for local feature branches before PR's.
git merge - merge the changes from one branch to another branch by preserving full commit history.
git rebase - merge the changes from one branch to another brnach by rewritting commit history.

# use cherry-pick to specific commit from one brnach to another branch.
git cherry pick - if we want to commit a specifc change to the branch then we use cherry pick.

git stash - saves the current branch changes
git stash list - lists all the stashes
stash@{0}
stash@{1}
git stash show stash@{0} - shows the changes that are stored in stash@{0}.
git stash pop stash@{0} -  applies the changes to current branch and removes the stash@{0} after applying. 
git stash apply stash@{0} - applies the changes to current branch keep the stash without removing. 
git stash drop stash@{0} - drops the stash.

# submodules.
git submodule update --init 
git submodule update -- recursive 
"git submodule update" syncs submodules to the commit referenced by main repository.


